claim.claim-text:
19. The method of claim 14 wherein the first and second configurations comprise wire including at least two portions of differing cross-sectional shape. 20. The method of claim 15 wherein removal of the first and second configurations comprises photo-etching. 21. The method of claim 15 wherein removal of the first and second configurations comprises cutting. 22. A method for manufacturing a retrieval assembly, comprising the steps of: forming a first loop from a first length of wire, the first length of wire comprising two ends; forming at least a second loop from a second length of wire, the second length of wire comprising two ends; securing the ends of the first length of wire to the ends of the second length of wire to form a retrieval assembly comprising a plurality of loops. 23. The method of claim 22 wherein securing the ends of the first length of wire to the ends of the second length of wire comprises twisting the ends together. 24. The method of claim 22 wherein the at least two loops comprise wire, the wire comprising a cross-section selected from a group consisting of round, oval, square, rectangular, and D-shaped. 25. The method of claim 22 wherein the at least two loops comprise wire including at least two portions of differing cross-sectional shape. 26. A method for making a medical retrieval device comprising the steps of: forming a basket comprising at least two loops ; inserting a wire between the at least two loops, the wire comprising a first end and a second end; pulling the first and second ends of the wire through a lumen of a cannula; and, securing the first and second ends of the wire to a cable, the cable joined to a handle, and the handle positioned at the proximal end of the device. 27. A medical retrieval device comprising: 

 a proximal handle; an outer sheath extending distally from the handle and including a lumen extending therethrough from a distal end of the outer sheath to a proximal end of the outer sheath; an inner sheath including a lumen extending therethrough from a distal end of the inner sheath to a proximal end of the inner sheath, the inner sheath axially moveable in the lumen of the outer sheath relative to the outer sheath; at least two opposing loops having a collapsed position in which the loops are collapsed within the lumen of the inner sheath and another position in which the loops are extended from the distal end of the inner sheath and out of the lumen, the loops being joined at a base and unattached to each other at their distal ends, the loops being moveable between an open position and a closed position with the loops being closer together at their distal ends when in the closed position than when in the open position to allow capture and release of material. 28. A medical retrieval device comprising: a proximal handle; a sheath extending distally from the handle and including a lumen extending therethrough from a distal end of the sheath to a proximal end of the sheath; opposing first and second hemi-baskets, each hemi-basket comprising a loop and a back stay, the opposing first and second hemi-baskets having a collapsed position in which the first and second hemi-baskets are collapsed within the lumen of the sheath and another position in which the first and second hemi-baskets extend from the distal end of the inner sheath and out of the lumen, the first and second hemi-baskets being joined at a base and unattached to each other at their distal ends, the first and second hemi-baskets being moveable between an open position and a closed position with the first and second hemi-baskets being closer together at their distal ends when in the closed position than when in the open position to allow capture and release of material. 29. A medical retrieval device comprising: a proximal handle; a sheath extending distally from the handle and including a lumen extending therethrough from a distal end of the sheath to a proximal end of the sheath; 

 at least two opposing loops including a collapsed position in which the loops are collapsed within the lumen of the inner sheath and another position in which the loops are extended from the distal end of the inner sheath and out of the lumen, the loops being joined at a base and unattached to each other at their distal ends, the loops being moveable between an open position and a closed position with the loops being closer together at their distal ends when in the closed position than when in the open position to allow capture and release of material. a base cannula; and an elongated member including a first portion, a second portion, and an intermediate portion, the intermediate portion of the elongated member inserted between the at least two loops, and the first and second portion of the elongated member inserted through the base cannula for securing the elongated member to the at least two loops.
